{{as|{{sti|'''Health'''}}|hp}}, or {{as|'''HP'''}} is a [[Champion statistic|stat]] that determines the number of hit-points that a unit has. [[Damage]] reduces a unit's health, and [[Death]] occurs when a unit has taken enough damage to reach '''0''' health. Health can be restored via [[health regeneration]], [[healing]], [[life steal]], and [[vamp]].
* Health '''{{tip|stacks additively}}''', and each point acquired directly adds to the statistic (1:1).

Every champion has a certain amount of base health that increases through [[Experience (champion)|growth per level]]. '''Maximum''' health refers to '''base''' plus '''bonus''' health, and is the largest value that health can be restored to, not counting [[Shield|shields]]. '''Bonus''' health can be gained from any source other than levels, for example from [[Champion ability|abilities]], [[Buff|buffs]], [[Item (League of Legends)|items]], [[Rune (League of Legends)|runes]], and others.

On the game HUD, health is represented by the green bar above the mana indicator, indicating the champion's '''current''' and '''maximum''' health. Units have different colored bars based on their respective markers. The player has a green or yellow bar (based on colorblind [[Settings (League of Legends)|setting]]) while allies have blue and enemies have red.

[[File:HealthBar.jpg|thumb|250px|Each segment of a champion's health bar represents 100 health.]]
Every unit and structure's health is displayed as a bar above their models.
* {{tip|Ward|Wards}} and similar [[champion summoned units]] have segmented health bars that each represent one life, but require another attack to remove.
* {{tip|Minions}} have a small non-descriptive bar.
* {{tip|Champions}} show a gauge on the health bar that illustrates the amount of health.
* {{tip|Monsters|Large and Epic monsters}}, as well as structures display an exact health count along with a non-descriptive bar.
* On {{tip|Summoner's Rift}}, {{tip|Turret|outer turrets}} have a gauge that represent plating, which disappears after they fall.

{{gold value}}​​​​​​​​
* '''Health''' has a gold value of {{g|{{#invoke:Gold value|wikivaluedefine}}{{#expr:{{#var:hp}} round 2}}}} per point.
