== Health as scaling ==
{{Main|Health/Scaling}}
Effects may benefit from (scale off of) a percentage/ratio, of '''current''' HP, '''missing''' HP, '''maximum''' HP, or '''bonus''' HP. Maximum health specifically can be modified by debuffs or buffs running out/being removed.

''For the full list of game elements that have a scaling with '''health''', see the main article above.''

== Grey health ==
[[File:Grey Health screenshot.png|thumb|150px|Grey health stored on the health bar, indicative of the amount of damage recently taken]]
'''Grey health''' indicates the portion of damage that was recently taken, stored on the [[health bar]]. It is designated for certain champions' abilities. Effects based on health do not account for grey health.

Champions with '''grey health''':
* {{ci|Dr. Mundo}} ({{ai|Heart Zapper|Dr. Mundo}})
* {{ci|Pyke}} ({{ai|Gift of the Drowned Ones|Pyke}})
* {{ci|Rengar}} ({{ai|Battle Roar|Rengar}})
* {{ci|Tahm Kench}} ({{ai|Thick Skin|Tahm Kench}})

'''Grey health''' appears dark grey on the health bar and between {{as|'''current''' health}} and any active {{tip|shield|shields}}.

== Health threshold ==
[[File:K'Sante All Out health threshold.png|thumb|150px|Health threshold as indicated on the health bar.]]
A unit that has a '''health threshold''' cannot exceed a certain amount of {{as|'''maximum''' health}} neither through {{tip|heal|healing}} nor {{stil|health regeneration}}. If the unit is above the threshold at the time of being affected by it, their {{as|'''current''' health}} is reduced to the threshold.

Abilities that grant a '''health threshold''':
* {{cai|All Out|K'Sante}}

